# A guest throws a mug into each of three tables: low at the near face (7 m/s), at mid height
# (9 m/s) and off its centre, so it turns (11 m/s). The host's world shows each table pushed no
# farther than the same throw pushes it solo, one world and no network.
scenario mug_table_100
scene mug_tables
seed 41
guests 1
settle 6s

net g1 rtt 100ms jitter 10ms loss 1%

p1 grab mug_a as lift_a
p1 wait 300ms
p1 throw 3.05 0.1 -2.4 speed 7 as throw_a
p1 wait 1s
p1 grab mug_b as lift_b
p1 wait 300ms
p1 throw 3.05 0.4 0 speed 9 as throw_b
p1 wait 1s
p1 grab mug_c as lift_c
p1 wait 300ms
p1 throw 3.05 0.1 2 speed 11 as throw_c

expect result lift_a granted
expect result lift_b granted
expect result lift_c granted
expect result throw_c done
# Derived margins, one a mode. A table leaves a hit at m v / (m + M) at most (0.3 kg mug, 6 kg
# table) and friction (sqrt(0.6 x 0.3), g 12) stops it over u^2 / (2 mu g): at most 1.1, 1.8 and
# 2.7 cm at 7, 9 and 11 m/s, growing with the square of the hit's speed.
# HOST, 0.2 mm: the host simulates the table, struck by its dynamic copy of the mug. Near the
# host's bodies the seam moves a flight no faster than the thrower's mug as played, driven or
# coasting, so it strikes at her speed to the velocity grid (1/32 m/s a component: 0.027 m/s),
# 2 x 0.027 / v of the slide: 0.13 mm at 11 m/s. Where it strikes: driven by velocity, the copy
# falls 1/2 g dt^2 a tick below its played path and its correction holds it within three ticks
# of that, 5 mm low; moving the contact 5 mm changes the impulse by 0.1 % (the mug's own mass
# bounds it) and the slide by 0.2 %: 0.05 mm. 0.18 mm in all.
# INTERACTION, 3.4 mm: the thrower takes the table (under the 20 kg light mass) at the hit and
# simulates it with her own mug, solo's physics less what her copy kept of the hit in that step;
# the host's dynamic copy follows her and is left as its world settled it within SYNC_SOFT_HOLD_M
# of her rest pose.
expect moved table_a <= solo 0.02cm interaction 0.34cm
expect moved table_b <= solo 0.02cm interaction 0.34cm
expect moved table_c <= solo 0.02cm interaction 0.34cm
# Every mug hit its table: a travel past the rest hold's 3.4 mm is no rounding of a pose at rest.
# (Under heavy loss a refused take can miss one: a missed effect, README "Contact claims".)
expect moved table_a >= 0.34cm
expect moved table_b >= 0.34cm
expect moved table_c >= 0.34cm
expect agree_at_rest 5cm 5deg
expect no_stuck
